<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover"><meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow"><meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer"><title>Activate your phone — Taptime</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/app.css"></head><body class="min-h-screen bg-porcelain text-ink antialiased"><main class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-md flex-col gap-6 px-4 py-8"><header class="flex items-baseline justify-between"><span class="font-display text-lg font-bold tracking-tight text-tappa-green">taptime</span> <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-ink/70">punchless</span></header><section class="docket"><p class="docket-label">Activating</p><h1 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Hello Maria Borg</h1><p class="mt-1 text-ink/70">Kebab Factory Ltd</p><p class="text-ink/70">St Julians</p></section>  <section class="bg-paper border border-line px-4 py-4"><h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold tracking-tight">Before you start</h2><ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-ink/85"><li><span class="font-bold">What a tap records.</span> When you touch the plaque, Taptime saves the time, your phone's internet (IP) address and — only at that moment — your location. Nothing runs in the background and nothing is recorded between taps.</li><li><span class="font-bold">No fingerprints. Ever.</span> Taptime collects no biometric data of any kind: no fingerprints, no face, no voice. Your phone's own screen lock stays private to your phone.</li><li><span class="font-bold">How long records are kept.</span> Your attendance records are kept for <span class="num font-bold">2</span> years, as set by your employer.</li><li><span class="font-bold">Who is responsible.</span> Kebab Factory Ltd is the controller of these records; Taptime processes them on their behalf. To see, correct or ask about your data, speak to your manager.</li></ul><p class="mt-4 border-t border-line pt-3 font-mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Non-production deployment: the retention period above is read from this server's configuration and is a placeholder value, not legal advice.</p></section> <section class="bg-paper border border-line px-4 py-4"><h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold tracking-tight">Join the Wi-Fi</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink/85">Connect to <span class="num font-bold">KF-StJulians-Staff</span> before you tap: being on the venue's network is how Taptime can tell you are really here.</p> <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink/70">You can skip this — activation works either way. Without the network, taps fall back to your location and may need your manager to confirm them.</p></section> <form method="post" action="/api/activate" class="flex flex-col gap-4"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="TESTcsrfTESTcsrfTESTcsrfTESTcsrfTESTcsrf123"> <label class="flex items-start gap-3 bg-paper border border-line px-4 py-4"><input type="checkbox" name="consent" value="yes" required class="mt-1 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 accent-tappa-green"> <span class="text-sm text-ink/85">I have read what Taptime records and how long it is kept.</span></label> <p class="text-center text-sm text-ink/70">This sets up this phone for <span class="font-bold text-ink">Maria Borg</span> at <span class="font-bold text-ink">Kebab Factory Ltd</span> .</p><button type="submit" class="tap-button">Activate this phone</button></form></main></body></html>